From: Proton CRM <noreply@proton.local>
Subject: [PATCH] availability menu: scroll a long status list

Since 0065 the sidebar "Set your availability" list shows the operator's
whole custom status catalogue plus Offline. DropdownBody's <ul> has no
height limit, so on a laptop screen the lower entries ran off the bottom
with no way to reach them. Cap the list at min(20rem, 50vh) and scroll it.
---
diff --git a/app/javascript/dashboard/components-next/sidebar/SidebarProfileMenuStatus.vue b/app/javascript/dashboard/components-next/sidebar/SidebarProfileMenuStatus.vue
index f218829..36fdc37 100644
--- a/app/javascript/dashboard/components-next/sidebar/SidebarProfileMenuStatus.vue
+++ b/app/javascript/dashboard/components-next/sidebar/SidebarProfileMenuStatus.vue
@@ -194,7 +194,15 @@ function changeAvailabilityStatus(availability) {
               </div>
             </Button>
           </template>
-          <DropdownBody class="min-w-32 z-20">
+          <!--
+            Patch 0100: 0065 turned this list into the operator's whole status
+            catalogue, and DropdownBody's <ul> has no height limit -- with a
+            long catalogue the lower entries (Offline among them) ran off the
+            screen with no way to scroll to them. Cap the list and scroll it.
+          -->
+          <DropdownBody
+            class="min-w-32 z-20 [&>ul]:max-h-[min(20rem,50vh)] [&>ul]:overflow-y-auto"
+          >
             <DropdownItem
               v-for="status in availabilityStatuses"
               :key="status.value"
